  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "For a rather niche use case of making your character behave like it is from an anime, or for recording performances in an anime animation style, a component like this may prove to be very useful, and outright required in order to achieve the target aesthetic. There is currently no reliable way to manage the \"framerate\" of avatar movement. There are ways to \"fake\" it by using parent constraints (with no Quest compatible method), however there should be a more convenient way to not only manipulate the \"update rate\" of the avatar, but to also sync it along with other avatars. There should be a limit where it begins updating normally, but lower values such as 24, 30, etc should result in a synced delay where if two users happened to choose the same framerate, they would update at the same moment. This framerate should be adjustable in real-time to mimic animation styles where variable framerates may prove to be incredibly useful, and can also be used to optimize physbone and IK computations so they occur less frequently.",
